---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import ProjectSlider from "../components/ProjectSlider.astro";
import {
  carpaSlides,
  droneResearchSlides,
  eddSlides,
  goatlabHighlightSlides,
  invenTeamSlides,
  irishSatDetailSlides,
  rfcSlides,
  summerClassifierSlides,
  summerMpu9250Slides,
  summerPcbSlides,
  vexSlides,
} from "../data/projectSlides";

export const vex_skills = ["C++", "Fusion 360"];
export const vex_awards = [
  "Excellence Award (State Qualifier)",
  "Innovate Award (State Qualifier)",
  "Design Award",
  "Judges Award",
];
export const invent_skills = ["Fusion 360"];
export const carpa_skills = ["Lithium Iron Phosphate Batteries", "Circuits"];
export const edd_skills = ["Soldering", "Electronics"];
export const irishsat_skills = ["C", "Python", "KiCad", "Arduino", "Electronics"];
export const irishsat_github = [
  { name: "IrishSat", url: "https://github.com/ND-IrishSat" },
  { name: "Helmotlz Cage", url: "https://github.com/ND-IrishSat/Helmholtz-24-25" },
  { name: "Goat PCB", url: "https://github.com/ND-IrishSat/GOAT-PCB" },
  {
    name: "Txt Writer",
    url: "https://github.com/andres-perez0/GoatLab-ArduinoTextWriter",
  },
];
---
<Layout title="Projects - Andres Perez" description="Online Engineering Portfolio">
  <body>
    <div slot="main" id="frame-div">
      <div id="main-div" class="m-0 p-0">
        <div id="textblock-div">
          <h1 id="header-tag">Projects ⚙️</h1>
          <p>
            Entering university, I would need to be prepared for the new challenges and projects I
            would encounter. So, I thought it would be a fun venture to learn how to make a website
            to track and document the projects I want to do. I was also inspired to start this after
            seeing how amazing my friend
            <a id="miguel-tag" href="https://github.com/Kaweees">Miguel VF</a>'s
            <a id="miguel-tag" href="https://miguelvf.dev/">website</a> looked!
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="textblock-div">
          <h1 id="header-tag">GOATLAB 🐐</h1>
          <div class="flex justify-between italic">
            <h3>Electronics Lead</h3>
            <h3>Sept. 2024 - Present</h3>
          </div>
          <section class="container">
            <p class="flex justify-center items-center my-2 italic">
              Swipe through the slides below to see highlights!
            </p>
            <!--
              First gallery on the page: `prioritizeFirstSlide` marks slide 1 as the likely LCP
              image (eager load + high fetch priority). Other galleries omit it so every image there
              stays lazy until the visitor scrolls near it.
            -->
            <ProjectSlider slides={goatlabHighlightSlides} prioritizeFirstSlide />
          </section>
          <div>
            <p class="flex justify-center items-center my-2 italic">
              Cage running a simulation below!
            </p>
            <!--
              preload="none" — do not download video data (beyond minimal metadata) until the user
              actually wants playback. That keeps large MP4s from competing with hero images during
              first load. (`preload="metadata"` would still fetch more than you need for below-fold clips.)
            -->
            <video controls preload="none">
              <source src="/projects/IrishSat/cage_video.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
            </video>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="textblock-div">
          <h1 id="header-tag">Fall 2025 Drone Research</h1>
          <div class="flex justify-between italic">
            <h3></h3>
            <h3>Aug. 2025 - Present</h3>
          </div>
          <section class="container">
            <p class="flex justify-center items-center my-2 italic">
              Swipe through the slides below to see highlights!
            </p>
            <ProjectSlider slides={droneResearchSlides} />
          </section>
        </div>

        <div id="textblock-div">
          <h1 id="header-tag">CREATE Newsletter 🫱🏽‍🫲🏼</h1>
          <div class="flex justify-between italic">
            <h3>Co-Author</h3>
            <h3>Sept. 2025 - Present</h3>
          </div>
          <section id="container">
            <p class="flex justify-center items-center my-2 italic">
              Scroll through a template of an Newsletter!
            </p>
            <iframe
              src="/test.html"
              class="w-full h-[500px] border rounded-xl shadow"
            ></iframe>
          </section>
        </div>

        <div id="textblock-div">
          <h1 id="header-tag">Summer Projects ☀️ - Hardware-Accelerated Human Activity Classifier</h1>
          <div class="flex justify-between italic">
            <h3></h3>
            <h3>May. 2025 - Aug. 2025</h3>
          </div>
          <section class="container">
            <p class="flex justify-center items-center my-2 italic">
              Swipe through the slides below to see highlights!
            </p>
            <ProjectSlider slides={summerClassifierSlides} />
          </section>
        </div>

        <div id="textblock-div">
          <h1 id="header-tag">Summer Projects ☀️ - MCU Data Logger 2 & 4 Layer PCB</h1>
          <div class="flex justify-between italic">
            <h3></h3>
            <h3>May. 2025 - Present</h3>
          </div>
          <section class="container">
            <p class="flex justify-center items-center my-2 italic">
              Swipe through the slides below to see highlights!
            </p>
            <ProjectSlider slides={summerPcbSlides} />
          </section>
        </div>

        <div id="textblock-div">
          <h1 id="header-tag">Summer Projects ☀️ - Live Sensor Data Visualization System</h1>
          <div class="flex justify-between italic">
            <h3></h3>
            <h3>May. 2025</h3>
          </div>
          <section class="container">
            <p class="flex justify-center items-center my-2 italic">
              Swipe through the slides below to see highlights!
            </p>
            <ProjectSlider slides={summerMpu9250Slides} />
          </section>
        </div>

        <div id="textblock-div">
          <h1 id="header-tag">Summer Projects ☀️ - Gravity Simulator in C++ using OpenGL</h1>
          <div class="flex justify-between italic">
            <h3></h3>
            <h3>May. 2025 - Aug. 2025</h3>
          </div>
          <div>
            <video controls preload="none">
              <source src="/projects/temp/twoBodiesInOrbit.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
            </video>
          </div>
          <div>
            <video controls preload="none">
              <source src="/projects/temp/fourBodiesInOrbit.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
            </video>
          </div>
          <p>Work in Progress ...</p>
        </div>

        <div id="textblock-div">
          <h1 id="header-tag">IrishSat - Goatlab 🍀</h1>
          <div class="flex justify-between italic">
            <h3>Electronics Lead</h3>
            <h3>Aug. 2024 - Present</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            IrishSat's Helmholtz Cage project has been a defining experience in my journey, providing
            hands-on opportunities to integrate hardware and software in real-world applications.
            Collaborating with a dedicated team, I developed a Python program to process serial data
            from a magnetometer and Arduino, enabling seamless conversion of magnetic vector readings
            into MATLAB-readable files. Under expert mentorship, I honed my skills in KiCad, MATLAB,
            and Raspberry Pi, contributing to iterative improvements in our Helmholtz Cage design.
            Taking ownership of circuit optimization, I designed a custom Arduino R3 hat PCB to
            compact circuits, carefully selecting components and managing footprints. Pair
            programming allowed me to support the final magnetometer driver programming, while I
            also designed a Python GUI to interface with a Raspberry Pi, enabling manual and
            PID-controlled magnetic field adjustments and visualizing dynamic field-time graphs.
          </p>
          <p>
            This project has reinforced my passion for interdisciplinary problem-solving and has
            inspired future goals, such as implementing PySol for coordinate-based field simulation and
            enhancing our PCB and GUI designs.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-evenly break-words my-2">
            <div class="indent-8 w-full sm:w-1/2">
              <h3>Githubs:</h3>
              <ul>
                {
                  irishsat_github.map((github) => (
                    <li class="indent-16">
                      <a
                        id="github-repo"
                        href={github.url}
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener noreferrer"
                      >
                        {github.name}
                      </a>
                    </li>
                  ))
                }
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="indent-8 w-full sm:w-1/2">
              <h3>Key Skills:</h3>
              <ul>
                {irishsat_skills.map((skill) => <li class="indent-16">{skill}</li>)}
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <section class="container">
            <p class="flex justify-center items-center my-2 italic">
              Swipe through the slides below to see highlights!
            </p>
            <ProjectSlider slides={irishSatDetailSlides} />
          </section>
        </div>

        <div id="textblock-div">
          <h1 id="header-tag">Robotic Football Club 🏈</h1>
          <div class="flex justify-between italic">
            <h3>Electronics Team</h3>
            <h3>Aug. 2024 - May. 2025</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            My involvement in robotic football in freshmen year focused mainly on practical
            application and skill development. I honed my soldering skills working on LED strips and
            took on the reconstructing the Pi Hat PCB that connects the Raspberry Pi and power the
            smaller electronics. This involved bringing the design to Git and creating and correcting
            the generated Bill of Materials (BOM) and Component Placement List files from KiCad.
            These files were then successfully exported for JLCPCB manufacturing, ensuring the
            accurate production of our component
          </p>

          <section class="container">
            <p class="flex justify-center items-center my-2 italic">
              Swipe through the slides below to see highlights!
            </p>
            <ProjectSlider slides={rfcSlides} />
          </section>
        </div>

        <div id="textblock-div">
          <h1 id="header-tag">VEX Robotics 🤖</h1>
          <div class="flex justify-between italic">
            <h3>Team Captin</h3>
            <h3>Aug. 2021 -Oct. 2023</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            VEX Robotics has been the most significant influence in my decision to pursue engineering.
            As a member of Team 687B Nerd Herd, I gained my first exposure to a STEM curriculum.
            Starting on the mechanical team, I learned the engineering design process, used CAD
            software like Fusion 360, and honed my skills in mechanical assembly.
          </p>
          <p>
            Over time, I was promoted to team captain, where I co-led a group of 12 members. Together
            with my co-captain, I organized team meetings, tracked participation, and drove continuous
            improvements in our designs and code to compete at a high level.
          </p>

          <section class="container">
            <p class="flex justify-center items-center my-2 italic">
              Swipe through the slides below to see highlights!
            </p>
            <ProjectSlider slides={vexSlides} />
          </section>
        </div>

        <div id="textblock-div">
          <h1 id="header-tag">MIT InvenTeam 🦞</h1>
          <div class="flex justify-between italic">
            <h3>Mechanical Team</h3>
            <h3>Aug. 2022 - Nov. 2023</h3>
          </div>

          <p>
            Although it was a smaller commitment, the MIT InvenTeam revolutionized how I viewed
            engineering. We identified a problem within the community, isolated possible solutions, and
            received real feedback from our customer base. Working with a team of 15, we drafted a
            winning proposal and secured a $7,500 grant as one of ten selected teams, focusing on
            design solutions for larger urban and tourist areas in my hometown. Furthermore, I
            practiced my Fusion 360 skills for the design and stress testing of critical Smart Walker
            components, including the frame, seat, and handles. I experienced firsthand the
            iterative prototyping of a product to refine the Smart Walker for presentation at the
            2023 Lemelson-MIT EurekaFest.
          </p>
          <section class="container">
            <p class="flex justify-center items-center my-2 italic">
              Swipe through the slides below to see highlights!
            </p>
            <ProjectSlider slides={invenTeamSlides} />
          </section>
        </div>

        <div id="textblock-div">
          <h1 id="header-tag">Engineering Design & Development 🔧</h1>
          <div class="flex justify-between italic">
            <h3>Electronics Team</h3>
            <h3>Aug. 2023 - Jun. 2024</h3>
          </div>
          <a
            class="flex text-center justify-center"
            id="github-repo"
            href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zvDc4tibHWs"
          >
            Watch the demonstration here!
          </a>
          <p>
            For my engineering design project class, we were tasked with designing and building a
            semi-autonomous suite of robotic mechanisms for use in exploring hazardous environments.
            To approach this, we broke the problem down into multiple components, and I joined the
            module group. In this group, I worked on the electrical aspects of the modules, where I
            learned soldering. For the actual modules, we decided to use an ESP-32 microcontroller
            with high-torque micro gear motors. We also included other components, such as a magnetic
            encoder, MOSFETs, and a TB6612FNG dual motor driver carrier.
          </p>
          <section class="container">
            <p class="flex justify-center items-center my-2 italic">
              Swipe through the slides below to see highlights!
            </p>
            <ProjectSlider slides={eddSlides} />
          </section>
        </div>

        <div id="textblock-div">
          <h1 id="header-tag">CARPA Racing Team 🏎️</h1>
          <div class="flex justify-between italic">
            <h3>Pit Crew</h3>
            <h3>Jan. 2024 - May. 2024</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            The CARPA Racing Team is a branch of the Engineering Design Class, where we had the
            opportunity to work on a race car designed for energy efficiency. However, safety was our
            highest priority, so we avoided making drastic measures to reduce weight.
          </p>

          <p>
            In this project, we replaced and maintained the race cars from previous years. I had the
            opportunity to learn about the car's circuitry and connect various components. We also
            utilized LiFe batteries. By physically replacing the disk brakes and motors, we were able
            to reduce the heat generated during prolonged use, ultimately increasing electric
            efficiency.
          </p>

          <div class="break-words">
            <p class="flex justify-center items-center my-2 italic">
              Swipe through the slides below to see highlights!
            </p>
            <section class="container">
              <ProjectSlider slides={carpaSlides} />
            </section>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="textblock-div">
          <h1 id="header-tag">Portfolio Website 💻</h1>
          <div class="flex justify-between italic">
            <h3>Developer</h3>
            <h3>Jul. 2024 - Present</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            This is my most recent project (at the time of writing this). Regardless, it is my first
            actual software project, and in all honesty, it's been pretty fun learning HTML and CSS
            with bits of JavaScript. I'm still a novice when it comes to frameworks, but I'd say
            utilized Astro and Tailwind CSS to a successful degree. The source code is linked
            <a id="github-repo" href="https://github.com/Reaper3629/Reaper3629.github.io">here</a> and
            below, and I do recommend people try making their own websites. It gives you a better idea
            of how other websites are structured and provides a platform to constantly iterate on and
            watch develop. As of writing this, I know it's a bit simplistic, but I am excited to explore
            other avenues of website development and see how I can update this site!
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</Layout>

<style>
  .container {
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
</style>
